<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Analysis and Results</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Overall results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across all query intents and configurations, just over half of the simulated final answers convey the forbidden composite. Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.1 Overall results ‣ 5 Analysis and Results ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows substantial generator variation: simulated GPT has the lowest observed overall disclosure, while Claude and Qwen disclose in roughly two-thirds of answers. Their refusal patterns differ sharply, and refusal and disclosure can occur in the same answer.</p>
</div>
