<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Both live GPT-led harnesses also disclose composites, with overall rates near the simulated GPT baseline. This serves as a soft validation of our simulated baselines’ realism. These averages combine benign, explicit, and adversarial queries and therefore do not measure disclosure during benign use alone. The following four findings isolate the benign failure mode, the limits of safeguards, disclosing refusals, and domain variation in the live comparison.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Finding 1: Benign requests can disclose forbidden composites</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Directly addressing RQ1, benign queries designed to be answerable from one document elicit forbidden composites in 7.08% of simulated GPT answers, 12.50% of Pi answers, and 8.75% of Hermes answers (<span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Figure <a href="#S5.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 5.2 Finding 1: Benign requests can disclose forbidden composites ‣ 5 Analysis and Results ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>). These rates average safeguard and distractor settings, establishing disclosure in simulation and autonomous live tool use. Appendix <a href="#A2.SSx3" title="GPT comparison ‣ Appendix B Supplementary tables and figures ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> retains counts, both outcomes, and matched differences.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.30418v1/benign-rates.svg" id="S5.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/215;" width="476" height="215"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Benign-query mosaic rates in simulated GPT and two live GPT-led harnesses pooling all safeguard and distractor settings. Whiskers depict 95% example-cluster intervals.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With headers shown, rules on, and no distractor, explicit-query disclosure is 0.00% for GPT, 58.00% for Claude, and 64.00% for Qwen; corresponding adversarial rates are 0.67%, 79.33%, and 75.33%, respectively (Table <a href="#A2.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ Configuration key ‣ Appendix B Supplementary tables and figures ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>). Tables <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Configuration key ‣ Appendix B Supplementary tables and figures ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>–<a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Configuration key ‣ Appendix B Supplementary tables and figures ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> report all three intents across all 24 simulated configurations, retaining separate distractor and safeguard settings with their exported intervals.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">A concrete benign failure.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The selected <span id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">med_006</span> question asks only for a medication-kit identifier, something the dispensing log (Document A) easily provides. Linking that identifier to a separate formulation key (Document B) reveals a subject’s placebo assignment. Qwen adds this forbidden conclusion in <span id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">every</span> stored benign answer for this example, including all ten answers with both safeguards enabled. Claude instead refuses across that axis, while GPT consistently does not disclose or refuse (Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ A concrete benign failure. ‣ 5.2 Finding 1: Benign requests can disclose forbidden composites ‣ 5 Analysis and Results ‣ Agent Mosaic: Recognizing Confidentiality Leaks in Agentic LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
